{"format":1,"seq":132,"writes":[{"type":"entry","value":{"model":[{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I'll use getFunctionDependencies on the pure, synchronous code, catching parse errors so there's simply no summary if it fails, since leading whitespace in the source shouldn't matter. For the result, the fitted value comes through as JSON in details.value, except for saveOnly cases where it's just the saved function with executed set to false.\n\nOn failure, I'll show the first line of the error as the summary and the full error text as the body, and for display I need to render values readably — strings as-is, objects with string fields shown multi-line and other fields as indented JSON, falling back to JSON.stringify for arrays or non-record values, and to the raw text content if details are missing entirely. For the call body, I'll strip any header from the code and show it alongside the params as indented JSON with functionId and saveOnly, separated from the result body by the same divider used elsewhere.\n\nFor the title, I need a required string, so when no explicit label is given I'll fall back to the first non-blank line of the program rather than letting it be generic. For header parsing I'll try applySourceOptions first and fall back to stripping the header line with a regex if that throws, then trim any leading blank line from the resulting code.\n\nThis new present functionality belongs only to the durable tool, so I'll put it in a new src/durable/present.ts module and wire it into createDurableTypeScriptTool. For the result summary, I'll join dependency ids with \" · \", and for saveOnly runs I'll report something like \"saved <name>\" using the savedFunction value; failures will be detected via result.isError, pulling the first line from the root error or error content.\n\nNow I want to check how tests are organized for the durable tool, and I should go read the test-audit skill before digging into the existing test directory structure.\n\n","thinkingSignature":""},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_bdrk_01RGHYiRqMG5spupBLpbHkr2","name":"typescript","arguments":{"code":"// @pit: {\"label\": \"Load test-audit skill and list durable tests\"}\nasync ({ workspace: { read, glob } }) => {\n  const [s, g] = await Promise.all([\n    read(\".pi/skills/pit-test-audit/SKILL.md\", { format: \"raw\" }),\n    glob([\"test/**/durable*\", \"test/durable/**\", \"tests/**/durable*\"], { limit: 50 }),\n  ]);\n  return { s: s.content.slice(0, 6000), g: g.entries };\n}"}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"nvidia","model":"aws/anthropic/bedrock-claude-opus-5-5","usage":{"input":2,"output":1346,"cacheRead":45724,"cacheWrite":1940,"totalTokens":49012,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0,"totalFromProvider":false},"cacheWrite1h":0,"reasoning":1128},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1794630861977,"responseId":"msg_bdrk_2wxvx5pdogoilqxrjhm3g55bvyjqszhzqw2nshh6blnsakg7oifq","rawStopReason":"tool_use","durationMs":17289,"thinkingLevel":"medium"}],"kind":"pi.assistant","id":59,"conversationId":1,"byTaskId":58}},{"type":"task","value":{"id":58,"conversationId":1,"kind":"pi.generation","version":2,"input":{},"background":false,"abortRequested":false,"state":{"status":"waiting","checkpoint":{"phase":"tools","assistant":59,"tools":[60],"pending":[]},"on":[60],"policy":"allSettled"},"startedAt":1794630861956}},{"type":"task","value":{"id":60,"conversationId":1,"kind":"pi.tool","version":3,"input":{"kind":"model","assistant":59,"callId":"toolu_bdrk_01RGHYiRqMG5spupBLpbHkr2"},"owner":58,"background":false,"abortRequested":false,"state":{"status":"pending","checkpoint":{"phase":"call"}}}},{"type":"document.change","id":2,"content":{"version":3,"kind":"base","value":{"run":{"taskId":58,"inputs":[8],"turns":13,"first":7},"tools":[{"callId":"toolu_bdrk_01RGHYiRqMG5spupBLpbHkr2","name":"typescript","taskId":60,"status":"pending"}]}}},{"type":"document.change","id":4,"content":{"version":1,"kind